WEBVTT

﻿1

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:39.183
Marriage has always been
a big deal to my mother.


00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.850
She loves weddings.


00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.018
Especially hers.


00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.682
And hers.


00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.093
And hers.


00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.260
And, well...


00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.362
you get the picture.


00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:14.207
But as easy as it was for
my mom to get married...


00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.810
Whee!


00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.379
my relationships...


00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.553
have never been
cleared for takeoff.


00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:34.228
I fell in love again
and it happened in a minute


00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:39.943
My eyes shot out like a fish out
of water and I'm jumpin' in it


00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.638
Oh, I don't hold back
No, I don't hold back


00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:46.240
I never stay within the lines


00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.514
I don't hold back
No, I don't hold back


00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.056
I'm gonna take what's mine


00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:56.221
Oh, don't get scared for me


00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.790
Just be prepared for me


00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:03.323
'Cause I'm in love with love


00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.732
In love


00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:10.537
When it comes to love
can't get enough


00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:16.473
I'm not gonna change, I'm not gonna
change, I'm not gonna change my ways


00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:22.776
'Cause I'm in love with love


00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:28.224
'Cause I'm in love with love


00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:34.596
When it comes to love
can't get enough


00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:37.395
Can't get enough


00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.631
I always wanted to be a
flight attendant. It's a great job.


00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.599
You get to travel around the world,


00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:46.610
meet interesting people
and see exotic places.


00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.146
But that hasn't left
a whole lat of time for love.


00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.145
My mom says it's
because I'm too picky.


00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.651
I don't think I'm picky.
I just know what I don't want.


00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.485
I don't want a man
with wandering eyes.


00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.488
Or one that cares
more about his work than me.


00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:07.762
I don't want a guy with
too much attitude.


00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.596
Or too little ambition.


00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.828
But I also don't want
to end up alone...


00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.505
living in a house
full of cats...


00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.673
smelling like soup.


00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.570
And I don't want to spend
my entire life...


00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.512
listening to my mother tell me


00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.545
how she can find five husbands...


00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:28.846
and I can't even find one.


00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:32.186
But she won't be able
to say that for long.


00:03:32.512 --> 00:03:36.517
A few months ago, I met this
amazing guy on a flight to Miami.


00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.022
His name is Graham.


00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.689
And I think he's the one.


00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:45.959
"I've had a change
of business plans...


00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:49.799
"...and it looks like I'll be spending
Thanksgiving at home in Chicago."


00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:51.872
"I know it's short notice, but..."


00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:53.633
Give me that.


00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:57.713
"... If you can make it, I would love
for you to join me for a weekend...


00:03:58.037 --> 00:04:00.017
"...you'll never forget."


00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.147
"Love, Graham."


00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:03.547
Graham is...


00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.388
Someone I've been dating
for a few months.


00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:11.595
- Wow. A few months? That's a record, Mo.
- Shut up.


00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:12.652
Ta-da!


00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.154
Montana! Buongiorno!


00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.731
Buongiorno, Taylor.


00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:19.561
It's zeppole. Italian donuts.


00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.898
Thank you, but I'm
watching my figure.


00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.835
Okay, but if you
change your mind, there's plenty.


00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:26.899
- Aw!
- Ciao bella.


00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.909
- Ciao bella.
- I'll get you some milk.


00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:31.743
Sounds great.


00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:35.018
She's so sweet.
What's with the Italian?


00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.585
She planned a trip to Rome
for our one-year anniversary.


00:04:37.644 --> 00:04:38.645
William!


00:04:38.745 --> 00:04:40.088
How do you turn your oven off?


00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:44.761
Oh! Okay, babe, I'll be right there.
I just put in a new oven.


00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:48.192
Of course you did.
Are you ever going to finish that place?


00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.196
- William?
- Hey?


00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.257
Got it.


00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.462
Aw, I'm coming.


00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.027
- Okay, good.
- Okay.


00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.364
I got to go.


00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.599
Yes, you do.


00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:57.864
Good luck in Rome.


00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.877
If it were me,
I would have chosen Paris.


00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:01.968
Hmm.


00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:03.446
So romantic.


00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:04.804
Good luck in Chicago.


00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:07.211
You think just because someone...


00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.946
sends me a rose, I'm just going
to fly off to whatever town he's in?


00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.621
Absolutely.


00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:17.291
According to my mother, you're not
a lady unless you're married...


00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.455
on or before your 30th birthday,


00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:22.558
and you're not a woman
until you've had at least two kids.


00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.463
If you Te not a lady
and you Te not a woman...


00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:27.960
you're like my best friend, Gail.


00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.466
Warm nuts?


00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.981
Oh, I'm so sorry.


00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.143
I got your nuts all messy.


00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:46.487
Sorry about that.


00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.325
That all better?


00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.592
Good.


00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.935
Happy Thanksgiving. Welcome.


00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.833
I could have been late, too.


00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:06.009
Remember 9F?
Boston to Cleveland?


00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:09.438
He invited me to his cabin in Vermont.
But I couldn't go.


00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:12.673
Why? Because I had to
be at work on time.


00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:14.507
- Happy Thanksgiving.
- Hi.


00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:17.618
Why are you working?
I thought you were off.


00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.017
I was. And now I'm not.


00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.347
Hello.


00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:22.516
Sam.


00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.720
I misplaced my badge.
Gail, could you check your cleavage?


00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:29.865
Trolling for men again, I see.


00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.294
Hi. Welcome aboard.


00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.634
So check this out.
A friend of my cousin's...


00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:39.343
bought a penthouse
on top of the Water Tower


00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.708
and he's having a party tonight.


00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.108
Lots of celebrities.
Oprah's supposed to be there.


00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:46.732
And Stedman.
How often does that happen?


00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.946
I have a plus one...
it has your name on it.


00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.488
Don't thank me, it's no problem.


00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.046
Wow, Sam.


00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:57.658
That sounds amazing.
I'd love to... but I can't.


00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.657
A person would need a hell of a
reason not to party with Oprah.


00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:06.996
Like dying or giving birth
or getting married.


00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.569
Cranberry juice.


00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:15.076
You're getting married?


00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.177
Montana is not getting married.


00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:20.577
If she was, being her best
friend, I'd know first.


00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.751
- I'm not getting married.
- See?


00:07:23.009 --> 00:07:24.010
Not yet.


00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:27.357
See? Does Mr. Not Yet have a name?


00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:29.186
Graham.


00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:30.925
Graham Jackson.


00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:33.357
5C, Philadelphia
to Chicago Graham Jackson?


00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:37.261
Blue Label on the rocks,
seven figures a year Graham Jackson?


00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:41.936
He could have invited
me for any holiday.


00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.763
Christmas, New Year's Eve.


00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.373
But Thanksgiving?


00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:49.436
Thanksgiving feels like... forever.


00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:51.704
- Yes, it does.
- You think so?


00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.142
There'll be more than
turkey getting stuffed.


00:07:55.208 --> 00:07:56.551
Such a hooker.


00:07:56.776 --> 00:07:58.619
Shut up. Does your mother know?


00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:00.983
No, and she won't
until I have a ring on this finger,


00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:02.993
which may be this weekend.


00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:05.123
I just have a feeling.


00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:10.791
I'm sorry.
Be right there with your vodka.


00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.261
Montana...


00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:20.501
when my grandmother
was very sick, she gave me this.


00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.074
I couldn't understand
what she was saying...


00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:25.342
she was in and out of
consciousness, but...


00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:28.649
I want you to have it.
It'll help you find true love.


00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:31.187
Aw! Thank you, Sam.
That's so sweet.


00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.083
I'm about to go.


00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:36.520
But before I do,
I want you to have these.


00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:41.088
Cranberry flavored
for the holidays.


00:08:42.855 --> 00:08:44.232
Go get 'em, girl.


00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:45.700
Thanks, Gail.


00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.565
These waters


00:08:51.364 --> 00:08:54.277
Can get a little busy


00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.307
But I've got experience


00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:04.278
Don't mind trekking
through the storm


00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:05.549
Wow.


00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:08.556
Graham, you've talked
about this for so long.


00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:13.887
I can't believe I finally got to see it.
It's absolutely beautiful.


00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:17.330
This is the first
time we're together


00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:19.231
in the city where I actually live.


00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.405
I wanted this to be special.


00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:25.635
It is.


00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:29.406
I wanted you to see a part of
me that most people don't.


00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:36.747
Look at that water.


00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:41.423
It just seems like it could go
on and on, forever and ever.


00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:46.760
That's what I felt
the day you walked into my life.


00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.159
And I was hoping...


00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:54.602
that we could go on and
on and on and on. Forever.


00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:56.604
Really?


00:10:00.533 --> 00:10:03.275
And ever since we first met


00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:08.848
I knew that I,
I knew I was ready baby


00:10:10.543 --> 00:10:13.353
To take that dive


00:10:13.546 --> 00:10:17.016
I'll be inside when
the tides are rolling baby


00:10:17.149 --> 00:10:21.598
You'll be at my place tonight,
all night


00:10:22.355 --> 00:10:23.766
All night, baby


00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:28.465
I'm not afraid to try


00:10:28.761 --> 00:10:33.073
And knew I, don't mind
playing in the rain


00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:37.379
And I was hoping that I'd get to


00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:42.549
Take that dive


00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:47.284
It's raining and I don't mind
if I get wet, baby


00:10:47.346 --> 00:10:54.321
Lovin' made you so wet,
your legs, your thighs


00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.433
And ever since we first met


00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.767
I knew that I


00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:02.328
I knew I was


00:11:02.662 --> 00:11:03.663
ready, baby


00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:08.009
To take that dive


00:11:10.002 --> 00:11:11.174
Sweetie?


00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:13.347
We're here.


00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:17.584
I thought we were
going to your house.


00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:21.848
We were. But I got an
emergency phone call.


00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:24.024
I have to fly to New York.


00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.696
There's tons of paperwork
I have to look over.


00:11:26.919 --> 00:11:30.526
I have to prepare for a meeting.
I'm sorry.


00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:33.202
I booked you in the
best suite in town.


00:11:33.426 --> 00:11:36.600
I'll make it up to
you when I come back, I promise.


00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:41.008
I could help you.
I could come with you.


00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:42.476
That's sweet.


00:11:43.269 --> 00:11:45.215
Let me just take care
of this business.


00:11:45.304 --> 00:11:47.011
I'll be back in a couple days.


00:11:47.373 --> 00:11:48.875
Then it's just me and you.


00:11:49.108 --> 00:11:50.382
- All right?
- Okay.


00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.555
Yes?


00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:04.066
Are you guys doing it?


00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:07.635
No. If we were doing it,
I would not be answering my phone.


00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:10.304
I would. So, how was it?


00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:13.733
None of your business.


00:12:13.966 --> 00:12:15.309
That bad, huh?


00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:16.569
I didn't say it was bad.


00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:17.908
You didn't say it was good.


00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:19.108
It was good.


00:12:19.238 --> 00:12:21.411
- Damn good.
- Then why are you on the phone?


00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:25.087
If you must know,
Graham had an emergency...


00:12:25.311 --> 00:12:27.655
business call and had to
fly out for an early meeting.


00:12:27.713 --> 00:12:29.989
Being a gentleman...


00:12:30.249 --> 00:12:33.253
he put me up at this amazing
hotel in one of the best suites.


00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:34.658
Girl, please.


00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:38.531
Montana, that man did not ask
you to fly all the way...


00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:41.731
to Chicago on
Thanksgiving to insist...


00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:45.001
that you stay in a hotel.
I smell a rat.


00:12:45.264 --> 00:12:46.265
I don't want to hear it.


00:12:46.599 --> 00:12:47.942
Hear what?


00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.943
That he dropped you off


00:12:50.002 --> 00:12:52.505
so he can dip his turkey neck
in another woman's gravy?


00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:54.445
Graham is not seeing another woman.


00:12:54.774 --> 00:12:56.117
- Prove it.
- How?


00:12:56.342 --> 00:12:59.016
Go to his house and
see for yourself.


00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:02.487
Gail, I am not
going over to that man's house.


00:13:02.548 --> 00:13:04.349
Do you know how crazy
that would make me look?


00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.193
Gail, I'm here.


00:13:06.452 --> 00:13:08.125
- Where?
- Graham's house.


00:13:08.454 --> 00:13:09.728
He came back and picked you up.


00:13:09.855 --> 00:13:11.129
Sort of.


00:13:14.293 --> 00:13:16.136
You went to his house uninvited?


00:13:16.362 --> 00:13:17.534
You told me to.


00:13:17.797 --> 00:13:19.367
I didn't think you'd do it.


00:13:19.465 --> 00:13:21.035
Are you kidding me?


00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:23.507
- What are you doing now?
- Going to his front door.


00:13:23.702 --> 00:13:26.046
Umm-umm. Do not knock
on that man's door.


00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:28.141
You'll look like a stalker.


00:13:28.374 --> 00:13:29.735
Right now you just look desperate.


00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:31.318
What am I supposed to do?


00:13:31.544 --> 00:13:32.648
Go to the back.


00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:36.991
Oh!


00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:47.664
Okay.


00:13:53.833 --> 00:13:55.506
What the hell was that?


00:13:56.702 --> 00:13:57.737
Hello?


00:13:57.837 --> 00:13:59.839
He's at the back door.
What do I do?


00:14:00.172 --> 00:14:02.846
Do you see a trash can?


00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:04.848
- Yeah. Why?
- Get in it.


00:14:05.177 --> 00:14:07.350
Are you crazy?
I'm not getting in a trash can.


00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.025
If I'm wrong about Graham...


00:14:09.248 --> 00:14:10.591
- ...and he catches you...
- Hello?


00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:13.194
At his house,
forget any future together.


00:14:14.019 --> 00:14:15.020
Get in the can!


00:14:26.265 --> 00:14:27.767
What are you doing?


00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:29.101
I'm in the trash can.


00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:31.036
Are you nuts?


00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:32.205
You told me to.


00:14:32.438 --> 00:14:33.610
Hello?


00:14:37.042 --> 00:14:38.043
Montana?


00:14:38.277 --> 00:14:39.449
I have to go.


00:15:20.819 --> 00:15:21.854
Yes?


00:15:21.921 --> 00:15:23.264
What are you doing now?


00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:25.262
Looking thru his window.


00:15:25.758 --> 00:15:28.762
Gail... it's beautiful.


00:15:28.994 --> 00:15:30.337
Any panties on the floor?


00:15:33.265 --> 00:15:34.903
No.


00:15:38.437 --> 00:15:41.680
He's preparing for his meeting,
just like he said he was.


00:15:43.275 --> 00:15:44.948
Gail was wrong.


00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:47.120
Graham was alone.


00:15:47.446 --> 00:15:49.289
And I was...


00:15:50.282 --> 00:15:52.455
right where I wanted to be.


00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:57.298
Sipping from the same mug.
Resting on the same rug.


00:15:57.623 --> 00:15:59.296
Just the two of us.


00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:01.298
And the kids.


00:16:01.627 --> 00:16:03.129
And friends.


00:16:08.968 --> 00:16:11.312
Toasting to our wonderful life.


00:16:15.474 --> 00:16:16.544
What was that noise?


00:16:17.209 --> 00:16:18.813
The sound of us toasting.


00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:22.556
No, that is the sound of
somebody coming in the house!


00:16:22.815 --> 00:16:23.987
Duck!


00:17:25.944 --> 00:17:29.016
Un-break my heart


00:17:29.081 --> 00:17:31.925
Say you'll love me again


00:17:33.919 --> 00:17:35.921
Undo this hurt you caused


00:17:35.988 --> 00:17:37.934
Oh my God.


00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.967
When you walked out the door


00:17:40.025 --> 00:17:42.733
And walked out of my life


00:17:42.795 --> 00:17:45.537
Un-cry these tears


00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:51.441
Montana? You want to talk about it?


00:17:52.204 --> 00:17:53.376
Go away.


00:17:53.472 --> 00:17:54.883
Hey.


00:17:55.874 --> 00:17:58.218
You've been playing
that song all day.


00:17:58.444 --> 00:17:59.889
Let's get something to eat.


00:18:00.012 --> 00:18:01.457
I don't want to get dressed.


00:18:01.713 --> 00:18:04.057
Okay, you don't have
to get dressed.


00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:06.561
But you got to get out
of this apartment.


00:18:07.119 --> 00:18:08.120
Okay?


00:18:09.455 --> 00:18:11.457
I don't have to get dressed?


00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:14.234
My cooking always cheers you up.


00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:18.105
A little wine.


00:18:18.897 --> 00:18:21.241
- Mo, you love avocado.
- All right.


00:18:29.141 --> 00:18:30.620
Look at that.


00:18:30.742 --> 00:18:33.154
Hey, vegan!


00:18:40.252 --> 00:18:43.995
We are so excited. We wanted
you to be the first to know.


00:18:44.256 --> 00:18:46.258
I wanted you to be
the first to know.


00:18:46.492 --> 00:18:47.493
After me.


00:18:47.559 --> 00:18:48.629
I'm engaged!


00:18:48.827 --> 00:18:51.831
Derrick proposed
with a two-carat diamond ring!


00:18:52.164 --> 00:18:54.838
I didn't get my first carat
until my third marriage.


00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:58.445
Montana, does this single rose mean
you're not single anymore?


00:18:59.338 --> 00:19:00.681
It's nothing.


00:19:01.006 --> 00:19:05.113
Sheree's fiance is taking us
all out to dinner tonight.


00:19:05.444 --> 00:19:08.288
I'm borrowing those earrings
I bought you for Christmas.


00:19:08.514 --> 00:19:11.859
Oh, yes, honey. I should
have bought them for myself!


00:19:12.184 --> 00:19:13.993
He's on track to break
the college record


00:19:14.119 --> 00:19:15.928
for most receptions in a season,


00:19:15.988 --> 00:19:17.194
maybe win a Heisman.


00:19:17.856 --> 00:19:20.200
You know I'm happy for
you, right, Sheree?


00:19:21.193 --> 00:19:22.536
But...


00:19:23.028 --> 00:19:25.702
you're just a
sophomore in college.


00:19:25.964 --> 00:19:28.308
You barely
know what you want to major in...


00:19:28.534 --> 00:19:31.310
much less, who you want to
spend the rest of your life with.


00:19:31.703 --> 00:19:32.807
Why now?


00:19:32.871 --> 00:19:35.317
Why not now? He's a great guy.


00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.886
And I don't want
to wait until I'm all old, like...


00:19:39.044 --> 00:19:40.045
Like me.


00:19:40.812 --> 00:19:42.155
I didn't mean it like that.


00:19:42.381 --> 00:19:43.883
What do you think?


00:19:44.883 --> 00:19:47.727
Yes? Fabulous? I hate them.


00:19:48.887 --> 00:19:50.992
Mom's letting me wear
her wedding dress.


00:19:51.223 --> 00:19:54.067
You can pick
whichever one you want.


00:19:55.394 --> 00:19:58.739
Only one thing that would make
this the best wedding ever.


00:20:01.033 --> 00:20:02.910
A bridesmaid again?


00:20:03.168 --> 00:20:06.911
I can't go to
my little sister's wedding single.


00:20:07.172 --> 00:20:09.413
I'll be the laughingstock
of my entire family.


00:20:09.675 --> 00:20:12.246
If you need a man,
I can get you one.


00:20:12.544 --> 00:20:13.625
Hey!


00:20:13.845 --> 00:20:16.849
Don't embarrass me.
It's not a man I need...


00:20:16.915 --> 00:20:19.759
it's a husband,
or a potential husband, in a month.


00:20:20.018 --> 00:20:21.520
Marry Gail.


00:20:21.587 --> 00:20:23.467
If she goes a week
without waxing her moustache,


00:20:23.488 --> 00:20:24.768
they'll think it's Steve Harvey.


00:20:25.190 --> 00:20:26.931
I'm serious.


00:20:27.192 --> 00:20:29.536
Why is it so hard to
find the right guy?


00:20:29.728 --> 00:20:30.729
Tell me about it.


00:20:30.929 --> 00:20:32.272
Tell me about it.


00:20:32.598 --> 00:20:34.942
A girl could have everything...


00:20:35.267 --> 00:20:38.976
an MBA, a J-O-B, but no M-A-N.


00:20:39.104 --> 00:20:42.608
That's because
men are intimidated by strong women.


00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:45.285
I never tell guys
that I have a degree.


00:20:45.711 --> 00:20:47.384
That's because you
don't have a degree.


00:20:47.613 --> 00:20:50.059
Sam, you keep missing
the damn point.


00:20:50.449 --> 00:20:52.793
I should give this back to you.


00:20:54.052 --> 00:20:55.395
It's hopeless with me.


00:20:59.291 --> 00:21:01.464
You won't show up single.
Give me your phone.


00:21:01.526 --> 00:21:02.732
Uh, uh, uh!


00:21:02.794 --> 00:21:04.967
Hang on. Now, look.


00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:07.232
She hasn't got time
to meet someone new.


00:21:07.366 --> 00:21:09.403
So why not revisit somebody old?


00:21:09.635 --> 00:21:11.478
But I don't even know...


00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:13.214
Picky is single.


00:21:13.272 --> 00:21:16.048
If we're lucky, one of these guys
has blossomed into Mr. Right.


00:21:16.908 --> 00:21:18.251
Let me see.


00:21:18.977 --> 00:21:21.321
She hasn't talked
to any of these guys in years.


00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:24.584
If she bumped into
one of them on a plane, she might.


00:21:24.816 --> 00:21:26.989
How would I know if
they were traveling?


00:21:27.252 --> 00:21:29.425
It's the holiday season...
everyone's traveling.


00:21:29.488 --> 00:21:31.866
And when someone
wants to fly, what do they do?


00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:32.991
Book a flight.


00:21:33.158 --> 00:21:34.660
There's Tanya in ticketing.


00:21:34.993 --> 00:21:38.338
I'm Tanya. Welcome to
TransAlliance. May I see your I.D.?


00:21:38.597 --> 00:21:40.508
Frankie in the Frequent
Flyer program.


00:21:40.766 --> 00:21:43.110
Thank you for choosing
TransAlliance.


00:21:43.335 --> 00:21:44.535
I turned them on to my hook-up


00:21:44.569 --> 00:21:46.776
at Louis Vuitton so
they owe me biggies.


00:21:47.372 --> 00:21:49.613
There's Calvin at
curbside check-in.


00:21:49.675 --> 00:21:51.348
Hi, I'm Calvin at curbside.


00:21:51.677 --> 00:21:54.351
Welcome to TransAlliance,
a flight you can afford...


00:21:54.613 --> 00:21:57.287
where your soul and bag
can be on one accord.


00:21:57.516 --> 00:22:00.019
And there's Cedric in security.


00:22:00.285 --> 00:22:04.529
First name, Cedric. Last name, take
everything out of your pockets!


00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.531
I need your pockets
out of your pockets!


00:22:06.792 --> 00:22:08.635
For the next few weeks,
any ex of yours


00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.637
who flies anywhere, we'll know.


00:22:10.862 --> 00:22:13.706
We just arrange your schedule
so you're on that flight.


00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:19.278
First of all, this is the stupidest
idea ever. Secondly of all...


00:22:19.338 --> 00:22:20.339
There's the degree.


00:22:20.706 --> 00:22:24.381
Assuming you could find out
when these guys are flying...


00:22:24.643 --> 00:22:27.317
which I doubt,
because it's your dumb-ass idea...


00:22:27.379 --> 00:22:28.414
Gail!


00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:32.553
These are all men you've dated
before, and it didn't work out.


00:22:32.818 --> 00:22:35.492
So what is going to
make this any different?


00:22:35.721 --> 00:22:37.496
Because this time, she's different.


00:22:37.723 --> 00:22:41.227
Same action, same outcome.
New actions, new outcome.


00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:45.167
Clearly, we have all
had too much to drink.


00:22:45.397 --> 00:22:49.846
This is illegal. We can all get
fired, and we can go to jail.


00:22:49.901 --> 00:22:53.246
Or we could come to the aid of
the sweetest...


00:22:53.505 --> 00:22:56.349
and most romantically
deserving human being alive...


00:22:56.575 --> 00:23:00.580
and help her find the truest
and fastest love of her life.


00:23:01.747 --> 00:23:05.092
We have thirty days
and 30,000 miles.


00:23:05.350 --> 00:23:07.261
To be brought up on federal charges.


00:23:07.519 --> 00:23:09.521
To find me a husband.


00:23:14.426 --> 00:23:18.602
I don't understand why you guys
think this is a good idea.


00:23:18.930 --> 00:23:23.777
It's the 21st century.
You don't need a man to define you.


00:23:27.939 --> 00:23:31.113
Everyone I know
is getting married and having kids.


00:23:31.376 --> 00:23:32.548
So what?


00:23:32.778 --> 00:23:35.122
I want someone to love me, too.


00:23:36.448 --> 00:23:38.928
Someone who thinks I'm the best.


00:23:39.017 --> 00:23:40.860
Who only sees me in the room.


00:23:41.953 --> 00:23:44.957
I know it might sound corny
or unrealistic, but...


00:23:46.458 --> 00:23:48.631
I know he's out there.


00:23:49.127 --> 00:23:51.300
And I don't want to
wait any longer.


00:23:53.899 --> 00:23:56.743
And you think you can
find him in 30 days?


00:23:57.803 --> 00:23:59.805
Of course not!


00:24:00.472 --> 00:24:01.644
Maybe?


00:24:06.211 --> 00:24:07.246
Hey Sam.


00:24:07.312 --> 00:24:09.314
- It actually worked.
- What worked?


00:24:09.581 --> 00:24:11.390
Our plan.
He's flying from Los Angeles


00:24:11.516 --> 00:24:13.325
to New York, connecting in Houston.


00:24:13.585 --> 00:24:14.928
- Who?
- One of your exes.


00:24:15.153 --> 00:24:16.757
Damon Diesel.


00:24:16.822 --> 00:24:17.823
One second!


00:24:18.089 --> 00:24:19.329
You've got to be kidding me.


00:24:19.424 --> 00:24:21.734
Damon Diesel
could barely take care of himself,


00:24:21.793 --> 00:24:23.101
much less a family.


00:24:23.161 --> 00:24:25.368
Google him. He's produced three


00:24:25.497 --> 00:24:27.670
number-one singles
in the last year.


00:24:27.933 --> 00:24:29.173
And he's Essence?
"Bachelor of the Month".


00:24:29.267 --> 00:24:31.907
He is looking for Mrs. Diesel.


00:24:33.138 --> 00:24:35.140
Hey! I'm on the toilet!


00:24:35.340 --> 00:24:37.513
Sam? I love you,


00:24:37.576 --> 00:24:40.182
- but I'm not getting on that flight. Okay?
- Montana!


00:24:42.013 --> 00:24:44.357
Oh, God, my mother
came over uninvited again.


00:24:44.683 --> 00:24:47.027
I will jack you up!
I will jack you up hard!


00:24:47.285 --> 00:24:48.355
I got to go.


00:24:50.021 --> 00:24:51.364
Montana.


00:24:51.857 --> 00:24:54.360
Honey, Mama's having a rough day.


00:24:55.026 --> 00:24:57.472
All this planning for
your sister's wedding...


00:24:57.596 --> 00:25:00.042
it's making me feel
like such a failure.


00:25:00.365 --> 00:25:03.812
Mom, five marriages
doesn't make you a failure.


00:25:04.035 --> 00:25:05.639
I wasn't talking about me.


00:25:07.305 --> 00:25:08.978
I started thinking...


00:25:09.374 --> 00:25:12.583
my youngest
daughter is marrying a wonderful...


00:25:12.644 --> 00:25:14.715
handsome, athletic young man.


00:25:15.046 --> 00:25:16.389
Yes, she is.


00:25:16.715 --> 00:25:20.720
And I might not even be alive to
see my oldest do the same.


00:25:21.386 --> 00:25:26.062
Anyway, we have to discuss your
sister's rehearsal dinner...


00:25:26.391 --> 00:25:29.395
seeing you are a
maid of honor again.


00:25:29.661 --> 00:25:33.666
I would love to talk about this,
but I have a flight to catch.


00:25:33.899 --> 00:25:36.743
Why didn't you tell me
you had a flight to catch?


00:25:37.002 --> 00:25:39.346
If you had called, I
would have told you.


00:25:39.571 --> 00:25:42.074
Make sure you call me when you land.


00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:46.083
I will call you whenever
I get to wherever I'm going.


00:25:46.411 --> 00:25:49.085
- I love you.
- Yeah, I love you.


00:25:56.421 --> 00:25:58.765
Sam? What's the flight number?


00:25:59.891 --> 00:26:04.203
I fell in love again
and it happened in a minute


00:26:05.864 --> 00:26:10.176
My eyes shot out like a fish out
of water and I'm jumpin' in it


00:26:11.703 --> 00:26:14.309
Oh, don't get scared for me


00:26:14.673 --> 00:26:16.744
Just be prepared for me


00:26:16.841 --> 00:26:22.814
'Cause I'm in love with love in love


00:26:23.448 --> 00:26:24.620
Taxi!


00:26:24.950 --> 00:26:26.452
Taxi! Taxi!


00:26:28.286 --> 00:26:30.288
William! William!


00:26:35.293 --> 00:26:36.636
Sorry!


00:26:37.462 --> 00:26:41.137
I have to get to the airport
fast... it's an emergency.


00:26:41.967 --> 00:26:43.810
- Somebody's looking good.
- Yeah?


00:26:45.236 --> 00:26:46.579
I almost didn't recognize you.


00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:49.649
Some of us like to update our
image every decade or so.


00:26:49.908 --> 00:26:52.218
This was the truck my father bought


00:26:52.344 --> 00:26:54.654
before he started his business.
It's vintage.


00:26:55.313 --> 00:26:57.088
I wasn't talking about the truck.


00:27:00.418 --> 00:27:02.420
You want to get to the airport?


00:27:05.657 --> 00:27:07.659
So what's the occasion?


00:27:07.726 --> 00:27:08.761
Oh,


00:27:08.827 --> 00:27:11.671
I'm meeting a friend in Houston,
then we're flying to New York.


00:27:11.930 --> 00:27:14.342
Why fly all the way to Houston


00:27:14.432 --> 00:27:16.844
to meet a friend
when New York is just an hour away?


00:27:18.503 --> 00:27:22.542
He doesn't exactly know I'm meeting him.
It's a surprise.


00:27:23.441 --> 00:27:26.115
Would this have anything to
do with Sheree's wedding?


00:27:26.378 --> 00:27:28.881
It has nothing to do with it.


00:27:31.049 --> 00:27:33.552
Okay, maybe it does. A little.


00:27:34.886 --> 00:27:37.389
My parents were together
almost 40 years...


00:27:37.889 --> 00:27:39.891
before my dad passed away.


00:27:40.558 --> 00:27:44.062
He kept the same job.
Drove the same truck.


00:27:44.396 --> 00:27:46.740
And stayed in love
with the same woman.


00:27:48.233 --> 00:27:52.409
Every night at six, there was an
oven-cooked meal waiting for him.


00:27:52.837 --> 00:27:53.838
The same one?


00:27:55.473 --> 00:27:56.816
Poor woman.


00:27:57.409 --> 00:27:58.911
You know, Mo...


00:28:00.245 --> 00:28:02.816
the magic isn't
in getting married.


00:28:03.281 --> 00:28:04.817
It's in the staying married.


00:28:06.418 --> 00:28:07.419
Yeah.


00:28:11.756 --> 00:28:14.760
William, I can't thank you enough.
Bye.


00:28:15.260 --> 00:28:17.262
Wish me luck, okay?


00:28:17.595 --> 00:28:18.938
I got my bag.


00:28:25.837 --> 00:28:26.838
I know, I know.


00:28:27.105 --> 00:28:29.949
- Your phone.
- I'm sorry. Bye.


00:28:30.375 --> 00:28:31.649
Hey! Hey!


00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:37.286
- Your earpiece.
- I'm sorry. You know me.


00:28:37.348 --> 00:28:39.123
Okay, see you later!


00:28:39.451 --> 00:28:40.452
- Thank you!
- Mo!


00:28:41.453 --> 00:28:43.455
Mo! Your lipstick!


00:28:44.122 --> 00:28:46.295
She's always forgetting something.


00:28:51.963 --> 00:28:52.964
Cedric!


00:28:53.465 --> 00:28:55.809
Nobody move! Back up! Nobody move!


00:28:56.134 --> 00:28:58.478
Sorry. Excuse me, it's an emergency.


00:29:01.306 --> 00:29:05.550
I have no life! Which gives
me all day to ruin yours!


00:29:05.877 --> 00:29:07.917
Welcome aboard
TransAlliance flight 143.


00:29:22.994 --> 00:29:25.099
Sam, I'm on the plane in a dress


00:29:25.230 --> 00:29:27.335
I can barely breathe in.
But he's not here.


00:29:27.565 --> 00:29:29.806
- Who?
- Damon Diesel. He's not on the flight.


00:29:30.001 --> 00:29:31.002
He is.


00:29:31.236 --> 00:29:32.579
No, he's not.


00:29:32.837 --> 00:29:34.407
This is ridiculous.


00:29:34.506 --> 00:29:35.883
I don't know how
you convinced me to do this,


00:29:36.007 --> 00:29:38.283
but I'm leaving. I love you, bye.


00:29:38.343 --> 00:29:40.584
I'd love to be the
stitches in that skirt.


00:29:42.347 --> 00:29:43.849
Montana Moore.


00:29:44.082 --> 00:29:45.425
Damon Diesel.


00:29:45.683 --> 00:29:48.857
- Wassup?
- Wow. Not much.


00:29:49.521 --> 00:29:51.865
You look great.


00:29:54.759 --> 00:29:56.102
You're in first class?


00:29:56.361 --> 00:29:58.363
That's the only way to ride.


00:30:02.367 --> 00:30:04.210
Okay, I'll be sitting down.


00:30:04.402 --> 00:30:07.281
Usually, I don't really
write about jewelry


00:30:07.372 --> 00:30:10.182
It's foolery, But something
about the way you look on my arm


00:30:10.241 --> 00:30:12.448
An arm on my neck
like you're my charm


00:30:12.510 --> 00:30:14.490
So, so fresh when we
step out at midnight


00:30:14.546 --> 00:30:16.583
Up to the spat we
chill and sit tight


00:30:19.217 --> 00:30:20.594
How long are you in town?


00:30:20.718 --> 00:30:22.061
Two or three days.


00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:24.600
I have meetings and family to see.


00:30:24.656 --> 00:30:25.896
How long are you in town?


00:30:25.957 --> 00:30:27.300
Long enough.


00:30:27.892 --> 00:30:29.565
Long enough for what?


00:30:30.061 --> 00:30:34.237
Long enough for us to spend some
quality time, if I'm allowed.


00:30:35.633 --> 00:30:36.976
You're allowed.


00:30:37.235 --> 00:30:39.579
Great. Let's go.


00:30:40.638 --> 00:30:41.981
Let's go.


00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:43.241
After you.


00:30:43.474 --> 00:30:46.785
I can't believe we
ran into each other. It's crazy.


00:30:50.415 --> 00:30:51.758
I'm busy.


00:30:52.417 --> 00:30:53.487
Damon Diesel.


00:30:53.618 --> 00:30:54.653
What's up, baby?


00:30:54.919 --> 00:30:55.954
Can I get you something to drink?


00:30:56.087 --> 00:30:57.088
The usual.


00:30:57.422 --> 00:31:01.097
A bottle of Chateau Margaux
'66, coming right up.


00:31:01.759 --> 00:31:04.171
You should think way
larger than that.


00:31:04.429 --> 00:31:05.931
- London, Dubai.
- Your check.


00:31:06.264 --> 00:31:07.607
Thank you.


00:31:07.832 --> 00:31:09.277
See you next time.


00:31:10.101 --> 00:31:13.446
Damon, I should
probably get back to my hotel.


00:31:13.671 --> 00:31:15.673
I have an early morning, and...


00:31:16.107 --> 00:31:18.610
a girl does need
her beauty rest.


00:31:19.777 --> 00:31:21.120
Real talk?


00:31:21.613 --> 00:31:25.789
You could stay awake the rest of
your life and still be beautiful.


00:31:27.285 --> 00:31:28.457
Thank you, Damon.


00:31:28.686 --> 00:31:30.688
Being with you tonight...


00:31:30.955 --> 00:31:34.368
you got a brother on
some till-death-do-we-part shit.


00:31:34.626 --> 00:31:37.300
Don't laugh. Why are you laughing?


00:31:38.529 --> 00:31:40.805
Damon. I've been
trying to reach you.


00:31:41.633 --> 00:31:43.670
Janine, Montana. Montana, Janine.


00:31:43.935 --> 00:31:44.970
Hi.


00:31:45.036 --> 00:31:47.380
Janine and her
husband work with me at the label.


00:31:47.639 --> 00:31:49.448
Can you call me when
you get a moment?


00:31:49.574 --> 00:31:51.383
